      "title": "Abstract",
      "gist": "The brain likely uses wave-based control, not just synapses, to flexibly coordinate huge numbers of neurons within fractions of a second for cognition.",
      "question": "Introduction — why can't synaptic connections alone explain the brain's flexible top-down control? (an argument from computational implausibility)"
    },
    "n0016": {
      "id": "n0016",
      "depth": 2,
