      "title": "Classical Model and Mixed Selectivity",
      "gist": "Classical models assume each neuron has one fixed function, but many cortical neurons multiplex several kinds of information at once, a pattern called mixed selectivity.",
      "question": "Mixed selectivity — why do neurons carry multiple blended signals instead of one fixed role? (evidence from prefrontal recordings)"
    },
