      "title": "Oscillations organize neural information",
      "gist": "Brain waves can directly alter nearby neurons' firing through ephaptic coupling, an electric-field interaction independent of synapses, making them well-suited for fast top-down control.",
      "question": "Ephaptic coupling — how can brain waves influence spiking without using synapses at all? (a mechanistic case)"
    },
    "n0041": {
      "id": "n0041",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0040",
      "children": [
        "n0042",
        "n0043"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-jnp59d",
        "spya-trb3jf"
      ],
      "title": "Oscillations organize neural information",
      "gist": "Brain waves coordinate activity over millimeter-to-centimeter scales by segregating spikes into different oscillation phases and opening temporal windows for communication, shaping spiking rather than merely following it.",
      "sourceHeading": "Oscillations organize neural information"
    },
