      "title": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling",
      "gist": "Neurons' electric fields can directly alter nearby neurons' firing without synapses, called ephaptic coupling, and because these fields spread continuously and near-instantly, they are well suited for rapid, large-scale coordination of spiking.",
      "sourceHeading": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling"
