      "title": "Spatial Computing: A theory of oscillatory control of neural information",
      "gist": "Spatial Computing proposes that alpha/beta waves act like changing stencils that suppress or permit gamma-band spiking, letting the same neurons flexibly serve different roles depending on context.",
      "question": "Spatial Computing — how do alpha/beta and gamma rhythms interact to route information flexibly through the cortex? (a mechanistic theory)",
      "sourceHeading": "Spatial Computing: A theory of oscillatory control of neural information"
    },
