      "title": "Analog Computation with Waves",
      "gist": "Waves can perform genuine analog computation, combining and interfering like physical signals to generate new patterns of neural excitation efficiently and in parallel.",
      "question": "Analog computation — how might the brain use wave interference, not spikes alone, to compute efficiently? (a physical analogy)",
      "sourceHeading": "Analog Computation with Waves"
    },
